1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,871
Did you find out
who the person helping us is?

2
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:40,457
<i>What does he want in return?</i>

3
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:47,255
He can do that? And why
does he want Chiara in return?

4
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:49,215
What he wants

5
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:52,427
is to overthrow
the President of the Philippines.

6
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,891
I just thought it would be better
if I took the initiative

7
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,769
and found out
who this agency's enemies are.

8
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,647
Tell me right away.

9
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,483
Because I want to know what you're doing.

10
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,821
He's not just some
ordinary guy, sweetheart.

11
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:14,532
Almost like the way
Donatello and I used to move.

12
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:17,077
I'm worried there might be
another threat coming.

13
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,828
Sweetheart. La Morte Bianca is gone.

14
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:20,163
So just relax, okay?

15
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,873
Nothing will get in our way anymore.

16
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:31,716
He's not just planning
to take down the Moravianos,

17
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:35,970
he's slowly building Sinigang Cartel 2.0.

18
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:39,808
So it's not just
the senator we're watching.

19
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:43,853
We're also watching
a new syndicate being born.

20
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:48,024
I thought you'd forgotten about me.

21
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:50,944
You really know how to drop a punchline.

22
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:53,780
I think you're spending
too much time with that senator.

23
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:55,740
So why did you call?

24
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:00,078
<i>And I hope you'll be honest this time.</i>

25
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,585
Will my family be left alone?

26
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:11,798
Did you know more people
get into accidents

27
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,175
than get killed by syndicates?

28
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,594
Norberto, don't give me that crap.

29
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:25,728
Of all people, you should know

30
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:28,648
that once you've stepped into a syndicate,

31
00:02:28,731 --> 00:02:32,861
you always have to watch your back.

32
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:45,582
That's not true.

33
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:46,958
Look at me.

34
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:49,168
I got out of that messed-up life.

35
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,505
Is that what you tell yourself every day?

36
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,554
You did escape
your messed-up life back then.

37
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:03,558
<i>But you know, it will catch up with you.</i>

38
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,685
So look at me.

39
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,856
I chose to stay in the service.

40
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,941
I chose to fight.

41
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:18,323
<i>I can't run from the wrongs</i>
<i>I've done in my life.</i>

42
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,241
So here I am,

43
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:25,580
facing my own ghosts from the past.

44
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:27,665
<i>Mario.</i>

45
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:31,669
No matter what happened between us,

46
00:03:33,212 --> 00:03:35,798
I still consider you a friend.

47
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:41,846
Not just as a friend, but as a father.

48
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,726
As soon as I get any information

49
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:52,273
that says there's a threat or danger
to Mikoy and Chiara's lives,

50
00:03:54,692 --> 00:03:57,278
you'll be the very first to know.

51
00:03:57,862 --> 00:03:59,364
Thank you, my friend.

52
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:00,531
<i>I look forward to it.</i>

53
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,254
Rahmboy!

54
00:04:16,297 --> 00:04:18,716
- Brothers.
- Whoa!

55
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,260
You're getting good at chopping!

56
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,637
The axe doesn't even get stuck
in the wood anymore.

57
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:25,390
Mario taught me, Mikoy.

58
00:04:26,891 --> 00:04:29,227
He said you can't just keep chopping away.

59
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,896
You've got to position yourself right
and know where to put your force.

60
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,441
And there's also a timing
to splitting the wood.

61
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:37,694
It's like dancing, right, guys?

62
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:41,155
- You need the right rhythm.
- What a punchline.

63
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:43,241
You know, it's kind of like life.

64
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:44,784
Right? Sometimes,

65
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:47,495
life is just life.

66
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:48,871
- That was lame!
- That was lame!

67
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:50,665
- Come on.
- What was that?

68
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,959
That made no sense.
I thought it was going somewhere.

69
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,756
Hey, wait. Why'd you stop?

70
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:03,219
No, bro. I was just happy for you guys.

71
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,848
You guys just seem so happy,
like you don't have a care in the world.

72
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:10,435
No, that's just how we are.

73
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:12,186
- Yes.
- That's how we were raised.

74
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,022
Not just by our parents,

75
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,858
but by our neighbors, our friends,

76
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:18,151
even the people we know.

77
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:21,821
And it's not that hard to be happy
even in the middle of problems.

78
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:25,658
As long as I don't have
toxic people around me.

79
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:27,243
That's the best part.

80
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,328
You guys are so fun.

81
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:30,997
I hope I get to experience that too.

82
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,084
He's getting all emotional!

83
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:36,085
So sentimental!

84
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:38,755
What, are you gonna open up now?

85
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:40,590
What, are we having an open forum now?

86
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:41,674
- Yes.
- Go ahead.

87
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,552
- It's just us anyway. We're all guys here.
- Exactly.

88
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,724
No, I just miss my mom.

89
00:05:57,398 --> 00:05:59,358
Where is your mother, Rahmboy?

90
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,529
She's an OFW, in Hong Kong.

91
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:05,740
Hong Kong, huh?

92
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,575
Chiara and I just got back from there.

93
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:09,827
We might've even seen your mother there.

94
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,080
That was five years ago, bro.

95
00:06:13,289 --> 00:06:15,166
- Is that so?
- Oh, five years ago.

96
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,085
So where is she now?

97
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:22,465
My mom.

98
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:27,136
Hello, Mom. We miss you!

99
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,971
Mom, I'm a size 10!

100
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:33,768
- Ma, I'm a size 7!
- What size 7?

101
00:06:33,851 --> 00:06:35,770
You guys, seriously. Here, take this.

102
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:39,023
These guys might ask her
to send them money next.

103
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,108
Thank you, bro.

104
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:41,609
Ma, sorry it's so noisy.

105
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:44,654
I'm fine. I'm with them.

106
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,575
- Oh, no!
- Why?

107
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,912
My fiancée left
her water bottle behind again.

108
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:54,413
I need to deliver it to her.

109
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:57,166
- What, is there no water there?
- Exactly.

110
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,501
You guys don't get it.

111
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:02,130
Her water bottle has lemon,
chia seeds, psyllium husk,

112
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:05,675
collagen, electrolytes,
ginkgo biloba, and Shirota strain.

113
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,552
If she doesn't drink that,

114
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:09,595
I'm sure we're all screwed again.

115
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:10,763
- We're screwed?
- We're screwed?

116
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:12,265
Of course, you're coming down with me!

117
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:15,935
Where's her water bottle
with all that stuff you mentioned?

118
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,019
There it is.

119
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:17,979
Let's find it.

120
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:19,188
Let's go!

121
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,857
Goodness!

122
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:26,988
Agent Alex, I'm so excited to see
Chiara wearing her wedding gown.

123
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:30,199
So this is what it feels like when someone
in the family is getting married.

124
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,993
You know, Agent,

125
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:34,245
I feel like I'm the one getting married.

126
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:35,788
Is that normal?

127
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:37,373
Of course, Miss Tess.

128
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:39,459
You've grown attached to Chiara too.

129
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:40,918
And you've come to think of her
as your daughter too.

130
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:41,752
Exactly.

131
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:43,838
So in a sense, it's like your daughter
who's getting married too.

132
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,339
Exactly.

133
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:47,967
Mom!

134
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:50,887
Mikoy, what are you doing here?

135
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:54,056
- Are you the one fitting the gown?
- No, Mom.

136
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,975
Chiara texted me.

137
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,810
She left her water bottle behind.

138
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,103
You know how it is.

139
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:01,397
That bottle is basically
her emotional support bottle.

140
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:05,276
She might transform if she doesn't get
to do her little water regimen, right?

141
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:06,652
Oh, right.

142
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:09,947
Miss Tess, Chiara's calling you.

143
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,617
My other daughter is calling me.
I'll leave you two for now.

144
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,043
Hey.

145
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,962
Thanks, okay?

146
00:08:26,464 --> 00:08:27,757
For what now?

147
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,218
Lately, you keep thanking me.

148
00:08:32,136 --> 00:08:33,054
For everything.

149
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:35,097
For being here.

150
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:37,266
For things like this.

151
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:40,603
Because Chiara doesn't always have to hear

152
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,147
my opinion, right?

153
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:47,068
It's important that she can talk
to people outside our relationship.

154
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:48,778
People who aren't my relatives.

155
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:51,739
Like you. Right?

156
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:55,743
So she can let out all the stress
she's dealing with in life.

157
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,703
Even if it's about me.

158
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:00,581
You know?

159
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,251
In short, so she's free to bash you.

160
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,337
Pretty much.

161
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,839
But I'm not perfect, you know?

162
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:11,842
Of course I'm in love with Chiara,
but I'm not perfect.

163
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:15,471
Of course, there are things
I might do that she won't like.

164
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:19,600
I don't want her to keep
all of that to herself.

165
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,854
You two really are perfect for each other.

166
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:31,779
Thank you, Alex.

167
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:39,078
Guys, Chiara's ready!

168
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:41,205
Mikoy, why are you still here?

169
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:44,208
You can't see Chiara
wearing her wedding gown.

170
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:45,126
It's bad luck.

171
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:48,254
Your mom's right.
Come on, Mikoy, go for now.

172
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:50,172
- Okay, just give this to Chiara.
- Sure.

173
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:51,924
Go on.

174
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:55,344
- Leonela, come on. Come with me.
- Go ahead, Miss Tess.

175
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:46,520
Oh, no, Mikoy! You're not allowed to look!

176
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:47,438
It's bad luck!

177
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,655
Did I come to the right building?

178
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:59,241
The place is right,
and so is the schedule.

179
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:02,328
But why does something feel wrong?

180
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:04,914
Did I miss an announcement?

181
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,375
You got that right.

182
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,794
You missed the announcement
that there's no meeting today.

183
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:12,797
I knew it.

184
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,965
So you knew there was no meeting?

185
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:19,428
I knew it. I'm the newest one
to get kicked out of the group chat,

186
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:22,556
then they made a new group chat
and didn't invite me.

187
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,892
It's so annoying. It pisses me off.

188
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:28,854
I've got your back.

189
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:32,191
I'll get updates from your classmates,

190
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:35,152
then I'll DM you if there are
any special announcements like this.

191
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:37,113
And you know what?

192
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,990
Sometimes it's better
to have fewer group chats.

193
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:42,159
Because think about it, all you'll see

194
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:45,955
is nonstop noise, gossip,
and spam messages anyway.

195
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:46,872
It's better this way.

196
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:50,042
Thank you, Laurence,
for offering to help, but you know,

197
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:51,210
I can handle this.

198
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:54,880
I know who's behind all this.

199
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,507
It's that girl.

200
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:00,136
Why should I adjust
when I'm the one being bullied?

201
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:02,304
And why should I be scared?

202
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:04,223
Just because I got
kicked out of the group chat?

203
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,062
Luisa Mae.

204
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,442
- So, did it arrive?
- It did.

205
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:34,628
Oh, sweetheart,
you look absolutely beautiful!

206
00:12:34,712 --> 00:12:36,881
<i>Your wedding gown looks perfect on you.</i>

207
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:47,433
One step closer
to becoming Mrs. Pinagpala.

208
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,813
And one step closer to the life
you've always dreamed of.

209
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,565
<i>A life that used to be just a dream.</i>

210
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:56,400
You prayed for it, and look at you now.

211
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,903
There you are,
already wearing your wedding gown.

212
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:04,408
It's just sad
that you're not here, Ma, Pa.

213
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,953
<i>I know this was a dream for you too, but…</i>

214
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,831
<i>it's okay even if you're not here.</i>

215
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:13,709
<i>I can still feel how much you love me.</i>

216
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:18,255
<i>Darling, I still need to make</i>
<i>some adjustments to your wedding gown.</i>

217
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:22,092
<i>I'm not satisfied yet,</i>
<i>and I'm still not happy with it.</i>

218
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:24,720
Oh, sweetheart, your seamstress
seems like a perfectionist.

219
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:26,305
That's a good thing because if it were me,

220
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:28,724
<i>I'd want every adjustment</i>
<i>to be perfect too.</i>

221
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:31,727
So have her fix it until
your wedding gown is perfect, okay?

222
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:34,104
<i>Yes, your mama is right, sweetheart.</i>

223
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,614
- I love you, sweetheart!
- I love you, sweetheart!

224
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:45,783
I'll give this to Mommy Tess.

225
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:47,284
‪And a little bit longer.

226
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:49,495
Chiara, Chiara, come here for a moment.

227
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:52,331
It looks like someone
wants to have a few things changed,

228
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:55,334
some things added or altered.
Alex has a few suggestions.

229
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:57,795
It's up to you if you want to, but
I was thinking it might look better if…

230
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:10,432
Where's Viktor?
He has a delivery from the senator.

231
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:14,270
Huh?!

232
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:17,147
Are you looking for Sir Viktor?

233
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:20,568
Why are you shouting?
I'm right in front of you.

234
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:24,864
When I was taking a shower earlier,

235
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:28,409
I think water got into my ear.

236
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:32,788
So I'm not sure if I'm speaking too softly

237
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:34,790
or too loudly.

238
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:37,960
Are you looking for Sir Viktor?

239
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,003
Yes.

240
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,171
Sir Viktor!

241
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:47,845
What is it?

242
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:50,806
Here it is, right?

243
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:52,391
<i>We're almost there.</i>

244
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:54,768
We'll officially be in-laws soon.

245
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:58,647
<i>After everything we've been through,</i>

246
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:02,109
our families really
are getting a happy ending.

247
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,903
<i>Thank you, in-law.</i>

248
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:06,447
For being there for Chiara,

249
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:09,742
while we're here, and I'm here,

250
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:12,786
<i>paying for the sins of a married couple.</i>

251
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:16,540
Thank you for taking care of her,

252
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:17,917
for listening to her.

253
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:22,254
For being there when it should've
been me, because I'm her mother.

254
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:24,590
Oh, in-law.

255
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:26,926
Chiara is like a daughter to me now.

256
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,553
You know, she's not hard to love.

257
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,640
<i>She's not hard to take care of either.</i>

258
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:36,435
Didn't I tell you?
We'll make it to our happy ending.

259
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:37,937
<i>And besides, hello?</i>

260
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,606
<i>Don't worry, I am so sure</i>

261
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:43,400
you'll see each other
and be together again.

262
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,778
Our families are getting a happy ending,

263
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:50,115
and you're going to have a happy ending
where you're crying and feeling sad?

264
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,333
Hey, Luisa Mae.

265
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:02,127
Enough with pretending
to be the sweet girl, nice girl,

266
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:04,171
and good girl.

267
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:13,305
And you actually brought a sidekick.

268
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:19,728
Seriously?

269
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,605
Don't you have any originality?

270
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:31,699
So you might as well know your place.

271
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:33,367
I'll know my place, all right.

272
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:39,123
And, you know, I'm protecting myself too,

273
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:41,709
and that's called self-defense.

274
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:44,753
And what you did
by kicking me out of the group chat,

275
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:46,338
that's bullying.

276
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:50,718
And I won't let you
just do whatever you want to me,

277
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,302
especially when it's wrong.

278
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:53,637
So, can you?

279
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:55,055
Enough.

280
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:04,523
Well, you don't get
to tell me when to stop

281
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:07,943
because I'm just getting started, Sofie.

282
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:15,075
Because starting today,

283
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:20,539
you, Sofia Anikka Ruiz,

284
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:24,001
are considered a persona non grata.

285
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,879
What the hell is a persona non grata?

286
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:31,383
Are you the city or something
and you have executive power?

287
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:33,177
Wow, that's a lot!

288
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:43,854
If you don't like the term
"persona non grata",

289
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:46,356
fine, let's make it simple.

290
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:59,828
You know, you really have no originality.

291
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,830
That's from F4.

292
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,629
You know what? That's enough.

293
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:19,139
You know, that's the price you pay
for messing with the queen bee.

294
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:21,475
And you know what? You're right.

295
00:18:57,052 --> 00:18:58,720
Okay, what's the plan?

296
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,681
Why do we have to be in formation?

297
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,685
- Nothing. Discreet matters.
- Okay.

298
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:07,437
Discreet? Why does it have to be discreet?

299
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:12,276
Because we're planning
your stag party, bro.

300
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:13,527
Right?

301
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:15,112
Wait, are you guys serious?

302
00:19:16,029 --> 00:19:17,281
No, I don't want that.

303
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:19,116
Why?

304
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:23,579
Wait, wait.

305
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,080
Then why is he still here?

306
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,290
- Exactly.
- This is a surprise.

307
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:28,542
- This is a surprise. You're not invited.
- Go inside, go inside.

308
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:30,460
Bro, wait. Go inside.
We'll call you later. Just wait.

309
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,964
Okay, here. Here's our plan.

310
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:37,092
Just keep in mind our budget,
1,500 only, so we can have more.

311
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,010
Yes.

312
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:40,053
- Is that possible?
- That's enough money.

313
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,681
Don't cry, my love.

314
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,352
Everything will be all right.

315
00:19:48,645 --> 00:19:50,856
We'll get out of here eventually.

316
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,360
I know.

317
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:58,780
I just can't accept that as her mother,

318
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:01,825
I'm not by my daughter's side

319
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:04,203
for the most important event of her life.

320
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:07,122
We won't even be able
to attend her wedding.

321
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:20,761
But we have to be happy for her.

322
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:27,434
So that she won't be sad either.

323
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,062
I know that.

324
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:32,314
There's nothing we can do

325
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,734
but be happy for her.

326
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:50,374
You need to come with us, Viktor Valtrovi.

327
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,211
- Take him.
- What? Why?

328
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:55,462
- What's going on?
- Where are you taking him?

329
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:57,673
- Where are you taking my husband?
- Where are you taking me?

330
00:20:57,756 --> 00:21:00,175
Hey, wait! Explain yourselves.

331
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,218
Come with us.

332
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:03,220
Where are you taking him?

333
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,640
What, aren't you going to answer?

334
00:21:06,723 --> 00:21:09,059
- Where are you taking my husband?
- Hey! What's going on?

335
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:10,227
- Don't worry.
- What is it this time?

336
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:13,730
- Viktor! Where are you taking my husband?
- Where are you taking Sir Viktor?

337
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:15,565
- Hang on!
- Viktor!

338
00:21:15,649 --> 00:21:17,567
Don't worry, ma'am.
I'll take care of Sir Viktor.

339
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:18,610
Sir Viktor!

340
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:19,861
- Viktor!
- Hey!

341
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,991
Wait!

342
00:21:25,158 --> 00:21:26,535
I'm Sir Viktor's plus-one.

343
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,996
We're like B1 and B2!

344
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,622
We're always together.

345
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:33,542
Wherever he is, I'm there!

346
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:34,835
Remember that!

347
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:36,461
Suit yourself!

348
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:40,632
Then you two can suffer together
with no relief in sight. Get in!

349
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:42,384
- Okay, okay. Easy.
- Go!

350
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:43,552
Come on.

351
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:50,267
So there we go. We're all set, okay?

352
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,979
Thank you!

353
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:57,441
So, Chiara, are you okay
with the changes we added?

354
00:21:57,524 --> 00:22:00,277
Of course. Actually,
I'm so thankful to you.

355
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:03,238
My fairy maid of honor.

356
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:05,824
Because I've really been nervous
about my wedding,

357
00:22:05,907 --> 00:22:07,659
but because all of you are here for me,

358
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:08,827
I'm excited now.

359
00:22:09,786 --> 00:22:12,956
I'm sure you'll be the most
beautiful woman on that day.

360
00:22:14,624 --> 00:22:17,419
Leonela, come on. Come with us.

361
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:19,046
Oh, no. You guys go ahead. Go ahead.

362
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:20,380
I still have somewhere to go.

363
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,090
I have something to take care of
with the catering.

364
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:23,633
Thank you so much.

365
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:25,469
- Thank you, thank you, everyone.
- Thank you. We'll go ahead.

366
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:27,721
Take care.

367
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:31,767
You're here?

368
00:22:33,643 --> 00:22:34,978
Do you need me to pick you up?

369
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:41,193
How about this?
Let's not see each other yet, okay?

370
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:04,049
Hey, Carlota.

371
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:06,343
What are you doing here?

372
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:08,970
Waiting for you.

373
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,680
Didn't I tell you to meet me here?

374
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:12,182
So we could go in together.

375
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:14,559
Okay, sure. Shall we?

376
00:23:15,143 --> 00:23:15,936
Shall we?

377
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:23,527
GLOBAL AGENCY FOR GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS

378
00:24:07,070 --> 00:24:09,156
Did you know it's been a while
since I last had a foot spa?

379
00:24:11,908 --> 00:24:14,035
<i>But believe me,</i>
<i>this call is an urgent matter.</i>

380
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:17,873
I have an update about that video
and that mysterious vigilante.

381
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:22,794
- Mario, Captain is looking for you.
- Why? Did something happen?

382
00:24:22,878 --> 00:24:24,796
It's about the Manananggal?

383
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,756
I'll just change my clothes.

384
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:29,593
- And I'll follow you to barangay hall.
- All right.

385
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:33,013
- About that again.
- And why the rush?

386
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,733
<i>Who were you talking to earlier?</i>

387
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:46,318
<i>What are you hiding, Sianong?</i>

388
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:49,738
<i>Why do I only see your red flags now?</i>

389
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:54,743
Mom?

390
00:24:58,205 --> 00:25:00,081
Mama Yaya?
